 ## Large-page scoring benchmark
 
+CUDA loads concatenate each DeltaNet input-projection group and each full-attention
+Q/K/V group after LoRA merging, then use one GEMM per group. CPU keeps separate
+projections. Set `VS1_CUA_S1_SEPARATE_PROJECTIONS=1` before loading the model to
+restore separate CUDA projections in the same build.
+
+The ignored `fused_delta_net_projections_match_separate_bf16` and
+`fused_attention_projections_match_separate_bf16` tests compare seeded random
+BF16 projections at the checkpoint dimensions with 1860 input rows. They print
+maximum absolute differences, maximum combined-tolerance ratios
+(`abs(fused - separate) / (2^-6 + 2^-6 * abs(separate))`), and differing-element
+counts. They also exercise fused whole-sequence and prefix/suffix layer calls.
+
 `wikipedia-56-options.json` is a captured native browser decision with 56 options.
 The ignored test loads the pinned local checkpoints on `cuda:0` in BF16,
 runs two warmup calls, then times ten `score_options` calls. Device synchronization
